    "available_at": "2026-10-21T18:21:59.309956+00:00",
    "body": "Lexus announced prices for its first fully electric three-row SUV, the 2027 TZ, with sales set to begin in the US later this year and in Europe in early 2027.\n2027 Lexus TZ prices and range\nThe new TZ is the largest, most luxurious Lexus electric SUV to date. It will go on sale by the end of 2026 in the US, and early 2027 in Europe.\nIn the US, the 2027 Lexus TZ will be available in three trims, starting at $64,050. The base TZ 450e Premium AWD model will be available to order in late 2026, followed by the Premium Touring AWD and Luxury AWD trims in early 2027.\nThe three-row electric SUV will be available with two battery packs: 76.96 kWh and 95.82 kWh. The former provides an EPA-estimated range of up to 253 miles, while the latter gets up to 315 miles.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nAll TZ variants come with an evolved version of Lexus’ DIRECT4 AWD system. The dual-motor AWD setup delivers a combined 308 horsepower.\n2027 Lexus TZ interior (Source: Lexus)\nInside, the three-row electric SUV features the latest Lexus Interface multimedia system. The setup includes a 14″ multimedia touchscreen display with customizable widgets, a Voice Assistant, and full-screen navigation on the digital cluster.\nThe 2027 Lexus TZ is 200.8″ long, 78.3″ wide, and 67.1″ tall, with a 120.1″ wheelbase, or roughly the same size as the Hyundai IONIQ 9 and the Volvo EX90.\n2027 Lexus TZ (Source: Lexus)\nThe base 2027 Lexus TZ 450e Premium AWD will be available to order later this year, starting at $64,050 with up to 253 miles of range.\nIn early 2027, the Touring and Luxury models will go on sale, starting at $72,050 and $80,550, respectively. Both use the extended-range 95.82 kWh battery. The Touring model offers up to 315 miles of range, while the most expensive Luxury trim gets 279 miles.\n2027 Lexus TZ trim | Driving Range | Starting Price *\nTZ 450e Premium AWD (arriving in late 2026) | 253 miles | $64,050\nTZ 450e Premium Touring AWD (arriving in early 2027) | 315 miles | $72,050\nTZ 450e Luxury AWD (arriving in early 2027) | 279 miles | $80,550\n2027 Lexus TZ prices and driving range by trim (*Including a $1,550 delivery fee)\nLexus said the electric SUV can recharge from 10% to 80% in about 35 minutes at up to 150 kW. It also includes an NACS charge port so you can access Tesla Superchargers without a separate adapter.\nLexus revealed TZ prices in several European markets ahead of its official market launch in early 2027.\n2027 Lexus TZ prices in the Netherlands (Source: Lexus Netherlands)\nIn the Netherlands , it will be available in three variants: 450e Standard Range, 450e Long Range Executive Line, and 450e Long Range President Line.\nThe base Standard Range model starts at 79,995 euros ($90,000), including a limited-time 4,000 euro discount.\n2027 Lexus TZ 550e interior (Source: Lexus UK)\nIt uses the same 77 kWh and 95.8 kWh batteries, offering a WLTP range of up to 280 miles (450 km) and 338 miles (544 km), respectively.\nIn Spain, the 2027 Lexus TZ will go on sale starting at 88,000 euros ($99,000), with prices ranging up to 105,000 euros ($118,000) for the top-spec Luxury two-tone variant.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on Twitter , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
